l be safe from attack. "],["pg",""],["ls","wcec"],["hs","nd"],["at","Eventually, dummy's diamonds can be used to discard South's club losers, "],["pg",""],["ls","ndsc"],["hs","wsnssses"],["at","but South must draw trump first. South doesn't mind losing 2 trump tricks as long as West wins both of those tricks. "],["pg",""],["ls","ssesws"],["nt","South should lead a trump from dummy at trick 2. "],["pg",""],["ls","ns"],["pc","s"],["hs","es"],["at","If East follows with the @S4, "],["pg",""],["ls","es"],["pc","s"],["hs","ssws"],["At","South should follow with a low spade from his hand, allowing West to win the trick cheaply. "],["pg",""],["ls","wsss"],["pc","ss"],["pg",""],["hs","whnh"],["At","West can do no better than return a heart to the dummy. "],["pg",""],["ls","whnh"],["pc","hjhahh"],["pg",""],["hs","nsssws"],["at","South can continue trump, playing an honor from his hand to force West's @SA. "],["pg",""],["ls","nsssws"],["pc","sssks"],["pg",""],["hs","wcscndes"],["at","West might as well cash the @CA at this point to prevent an overtrick (as South is now in a position to draw East's last trump and run the diamonds)."],["pg",""],["up","11"],["ls","esscwcnd"],["hs","esssws"],["nt","If East plays the @S9, @S10, or @SJ on the first round of trump, South must cover with the @SK or @SQ to force West's @SA. "],["pg",""],["ls","esssws"],["pc","stsksa"],["pg",""],["hs","whnh"],["at","West returns a heart to the dummy "],["pg",""],["ls","whnh"],["pc","hjhahh"],["pg",""],["hs","nses"],["at","and East follows with the @S4 on the second round of trump. "],["pg",""],["ls","esns"],["pc","ss"],["hs","ssws"],["at","South should play a low spade on this trick to make sure that West wins the second trump trick for the defense. "],["pg",""],["ls","ssws"],["pc","ss"],["pg",""],["hs","wcndessssc"],["at","As before, West must cash the @CA to prevent an overtrick. Otherwise, South would be able to draw East's last trump and run diamonds to discard his clubs."],["",""]]}}